File Index

Sub-components + hooks for AutoLevelingWizard.tsx (the wizard that replaces AutoLevelingModal).

/useCharacterLevel.ts
Purpose: useCharacterLogin() — the connected character's level + name from GMCP login_data (game:character-login event + __SA_EVENT_SNAPSHOTS__ for late subscribers).

/useWizardDraft.ts
Purpose: useWizardDraft() — in-memory wizard draft (areaSlug, area detail, DraftTarget[], mode, playerClass, initiationCommand, buffs, fightCommands, playerAlignment — default 'neutral'; the MOB's alignment is engine-detected from auras, not in the draft; startRoom — 2026-09-12, an editable Review-step reminder seeded from area.startRoom, purely informational; restStartOfRound/restEndOfRound — semicolon-separated command text, 2026-09-12 — + restDuringRound: AutoLevelRestDuringRoundRule[]; weightAtOrAbovePct/weightCommands — 2026-09-13, weightCommands also semicolon-separated text, no separate enable flag — a blank weightCommands list IS off, the checkbox was dropped same day per live-playtest feedback) + actions (setArea, toggleTarget, addCustomTarget, removeCustomTarget, patch, reset). Not persisted until Start builds the AutoLevelConfig.

/AreaStep.tsx
Purpose: Step 1 — area list from autoleveling-content.getAreaIndex() grouped by continent, search box, a min/max Level range gate (seeded ±5 from GMCP level once, then user-owned; areasForLevelRange overlaps with a ±4 margin and drops "range not set" areas), level-match dot + in-band L-range highlight when connected, ★ for IsExcellentLevelingArea, per-row L-range/steps/targets ("level range not set" when span ≥ 40), "Custom path…" fallthrough row.

/TargetsStep.tsx
Purpose: Step 2 — recommended targets (from the area detail) pre-checked with level badge + kill keyword; separate "Your targets" list for user additions; manual add row (look description + kill keyword). Toggle/add/remove flow up to the wizard which persists customs to autoleveling-user-data.

/CombatStep.tsx
Purpose: Step 3 — class selector (served catalog via getClassCatalog(), base classes then a "Reclasses" optgroup, DSL_CLASSES_FALLBACK only if the catalog is empty → setPrefs + reloads that class's fight overlay), read-only level/name from useCharacterLogin, engage-command input, one Good/Neutral/Evil "Your alignment" AlignPick (persists via setPrefs; the mob's alignment is read live from auras by the engine), a pre-round buff editor and a per-class fight-command rotation. 2026-09-13 rewrite of both catalog pickers: both use `FilterableSelect` (typeahead, alphabetized, replaces the native `<select>`+`<optgroup>`). First pass had the buff picker show a hardcoded BUFF_CATALOG unconditionally alongside the class's own group-filtered spells (leaking e.g. Shukenja-only spells into every class's list) — fixed, then REPLACED entirely same day: the buff picker now shows every ability the selected class actually has (`abilitiesForClass`, no group filtering), grouped by type (Skills/Spells/Songs headers) — no more generic catalog fallback, no more group-heuristic guessing which abilities count as "buffs" (that heuristic kept being wrong; see autoleveling-classes.ts's `.annotated`). `addClassBuff` still cross-references BUFF_CATALOG by name for a verified cmd+affect when available; otherwise seeds an `unverified: true` guess — a skill guesses a bare command + tick-gate (skills rarely register a GMCP affect), a spell/song guesses `cast '<name>'` + an affect-name gate. Fight section's "Add ability" picker (classOffensiveAbilities → skill = bare name, spell = `cast '<name>' {name}`, UNCHANGED — still group-filtered) got the same FilterableSelect + alphabetize treatment — 2026-09-12: pre-fills cooldownSec from autoleveling-user-data's getLearnedCooldown(cmd) instead of always 0. 3-way gate segmented control per buff (affect drops / every N ticks / every round) + affect-gated inCombatCmd + holdNearLevel unchanged. 2026-09-12 additions on every buff card AND fight-command row (the latter restructured from a bare .editorRow into a .buffCard so there's room): shared `VitalsGateControl` (checkbox + hp/mp/stamina dropdown + below/above toggle + %% input → BuffRow/FightRow.vitalsGate) and `OnceGateControl` (no limit / once per round / once per fight → .onceKey). Debounce-saves to autoleveling-user-data; the wizard seeds the draft from those stores on area selection. 2026-09-13: added `ReorderButtons` (shared ↑/↓ `.iconButton` pair) to every buff card and fight-command row — `moveItem()` swaps the row with its adjacent neighbor and re-commits the array, since execution order IS list order (buffs cast top-to-bottom in `steps.start.pre`, fight commands sent top-to-bottom in `steps.fight.exec` — see `draftToConfig`) and there was previously no way to change it without deleting and re-adding rows.

/FilterableSelect.tsx
Purpose: New 2026-09-13 — a text-input typeahead that behaves like a `<select>` for the caller (one `onPick(value)` on commit) but filters a flat option list live-as-you-type instead of a native dropdown; consecutive options sharing a `group` get one header, mirroring `<optgroup>`. Callers alphabetize before passing options in (this component preserves given order). Used by CombatStep.tsx's buff-add and fight-command-add pickers.

/RestStep.tsx
Purpose: Step 4 (new, 2026-09-12) — Rest. Two plain-text fields (restStartOfRound "wake up", restEndOfRound "rest", both semicolon-separated for multiple commands, same join convention as fullRoute) + a repeatable during-round rule card (HP/MP/Stamina ≤ threshold, all optional and AND'd together per rule — the user's own example is "HP below 50% AND mana below 50%" — plus a recover-to ≥ target per stat), reusing the buff-card/gateBar styling from CombatStep. All rest behavior is out-of-combat only, enforced by the engine (autoleveling-engine.ts checkDuringRoundRest), not this UI. 2026-09-13 (live-playtest fix): both fields now go through the alias/script "command processor" (RuntimeSingleton.Runtime.executeAlias, via a new deps.sendThroughCommandProcessor), not a raw literal send — a rest sequence built as the player's own alias/macro was being sent to the MUD verbatim and silently doing nothing. Same convention now applies to the during-round rules below since they reuse these exact two fields.

/WeightStep.tsx
Purpose: Step 5 (new, 2026-09-13) — Weight, between Rest and Review. Two unconditional fields: a threshold-percentage number input and a semicolon-separated commands text field, same convention as Rest's fields. NO enable checkbox (removed same day, live-playtest feedback: "not a simple checkbox") — a blank commands field IS off, same convention Rest's own start/end-of-round fields already used. Out-of-combat only, enforced by the engine (autoleveling-engine.ts checkWeightGate — gates on `commands.length`, not a separate flag), not this UI — fires the drop sequence once per threshold crossing (edge-triggered).

/ReviewStep.tsx
Purpose: Step 6 (was step 5 before WeightStep was inserted, 2026-09-13; step 4 before RestStep, 2026-09-12) — mostly read-only plain-language summary of the draft (area + level range + ★, an editable "Start room" reminder text field seeded from area.startRoom, fullRoute() step count with a "Show steps" disclosure listing every command — explicit `{i+1}.` text rather than a native `<ol>`, whose counter rendered wrong inside the scrolling container, cause not fully diagnosed — enabled/total targets as a collapsible `{lookName} ({engageName})` list, class, alignment row (no "you" prefix — just the alignment + the aura-detection note), engage command, buff list with per-row gate/in-combat/hold-near-level via describeBuffGate() + an "unverified" flag, fight-command list with cooldowns, a Rest row summarizing both command lists + every during-round rule in plain language, a Weight row ("drop at N% carry weight: <commands>" or "off"), mode + loop). No config is built here — that happens on Start.

/dsl-classes.ts
Purpose: DSL_CLASSES_FALLBACK — just the 5 base class names, a last-resort static list for CombatStep's class picker when the served catalog (autoleveling-classes) is unreachable AND its offline JSON is empty. The real list comes from GET /maps/autoleveling/classes.
